1A. In this Notification —
“explosive” has the meaning given by section 4(1) of the GEWC Act;
“GEWC Act” means the Guns, Explosives and Weapons Control Act 2021;
“gun” has the meaning given by section 3 of the GEWC Act;
“gun accessory” has the meaning given by section 3(5) of the GEWC Act;
“licensee” has the meaning given by section 2(1) of the GEWC Act.
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]

2. For the purposes of section 263 of the Code (report of qualified persons), each of the following persons is a “qualified person”:
(a)any inspector of weights and measures duly appointed as such under the provisions of any written law;
(b)any officer of consumer protection duly appointed as such under the provisions of any written law;
(c)any pathologist;
(d)any medical practitioner who conducts post-mortem examination under the supervision of a pathologist;
(e)any Health Sciences Authority officer who undertakes scientific analytical work;
(f)the Government Bacteriologist;
(g)the Commissioner of Parks and Recreation;
(h)any person appointed by the Minister to be a document examiner;
(i)any Armament Management Manager (Armament & Automotive Management Division) of the Police Logistics Department of the Singapore Police Force;
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]
(j)the Assistant Director (Armament & Automotive Management Division) of the Police Logistics Department of the Singapore Police Force;
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]
(k)the Head Armament Management (Armament & Automotive Management Division) of the Police Logistics Department of the Singapore Police Force;
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]
(l)any officer of the Home Team Science and Technology Agency who assists the Singapore Police Force in the examination of any gun, gun accessory or explosive;
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]
(la)any employee of a licensee who is assigned by the licensee to assist the Singapore Police Force in the examination of any gun, gun accessory or explosive;
[S 425/2025 wef 01/07/2025]
(m)any fingerprint examiner, computer forensic examiner or crime scene examiner of the Singapore Police Force;
(n)any officer of the Immigration & Checkpoints Authority who assists the Singapore Police Force in the examination and verification of any document issued by the Immigration & Checkpoints Authority;
(o)any radiologist or radiotherapist of the Medical Service;
(p)any Forensic Science Officer of the Ministry of Defence;
(q)any registered medical practitioner under the Medical Registration Act (Cap. 174) employed in the Histopathology Section of Singapore General Hospital Pte. Ltd.;
[S 771/2019 wef 25/11/2019]
(r)any Ministry of Health officer who undertakes scientific analytical work;
[S 771/2019 wef 25/11/2019]
(s)any Casino Gaming Expert (Casino Crime Investigation Branch) of the Singapore Police Force;
[S 771/2019 wef 25/11/2019]
(t)any Gambling Expert (Specialised Crime Branch) of the Singapore Police Force;
[S 771/2019 wef 25/11/2019]
(u)any Triad Expert (Secret Societies Branch) of the Singapore Police Force.
[S 771/2019 wef 25/11/2019]
